---
// Vault Local — the PrismVault product, bundled inside the viewer's installer
// (owner decision 2026-10-05, Launch-Manager DISPATCH-2026-10-05-three-products §4b).
//
// There is no download form here on purpose: Vault Local ships inside the
// MyBodyPrism installer, so /pricing is the one download page for both.
//
// The privacy paragraph below is the owner's APPROVED wording, verified
// 2026-10-05, and it is the ceiling on what this page may claim. Do not widen
// it, and do not reword it. The one-time licence check it mentions belongs to
// the VIEWER; the Vault itself makes no outbound call at all.
//
// Every other claim here was read in PrismVault's own source on 2026-10-05:
//   - binds 127.0.0.1 only           src/prismvault/app_runtime.py:81
//   - local-only host allow-list     src/prismvault/api.py:310
//   - encrypted database (SQLCipher) src/prismvault/db.py, crypto.py
//   - recovery key shown once        src/prismvault/crypto.py:12
//   - no outbound HTTP client in src/prismvault
// If any of those change, this page changes with them.
import Layout from "../layouts/Default.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Vault Local — MyBodyPrism"
  description="Vault Local keeps your scans and records on your own computer, in an encrypted store, with no account to create. Included free with the MyBodyPrism viewer."
>
  <section class="container narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Included free</p>
    <h1>Vault Local</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      A place on your own computer to keep your scans and records together —
      encrypted, searchable, and yours. It is installed with the MyBodyPrism
      viewer, and there is no account to create.
    </p>

    <h2>Your records stay with you</h2>
    <p class="claim">
      Your scans and records never leave your computer. The only thing that ever
      goes out is a one-time licence check, which carries no health data.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      That licence check belongs to the viewer. Vault Local itself makes no
      network call at all.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul class="points">
      <li>
        <strong>It runs on your machine.</strong> Starting Vault Local runs a
        small server on your own computer and opens its pages in your browser.
        Nothing is hosted by us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No account, no sign-in, no network.</strong> First run needs none
        of them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The store is encrypted on disk.</strong> Your vault database is
        encrypted where it sits, not just protected by your Windows login.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One recovery key, shown once.</strong> You are shown a recovery
        key when the vault is created, and it is never written to a file for
        you. Keep it somewhere safe — it is how you get back in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Free, with no fixed end date.</strong> See the
        <a href="/legal/eula">EULA</a> for the licence terms.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Getting it</h2>
    <p>
      Vault Local is part of the MyBodyPrism installer — install the viewer and
      the Vault is there, with its own entry in your Start menu. See
      <a href="/pricing">the download page</a> and the
      <a href="/system-requirements">system requirements</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      Vault Local is for keeping and reviewing your own records. It is not a
      medical device, and it is not for diagnosis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .narrow { max-width: 760px; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
    .eyebrow {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      color: var(--c-brand);
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--c-text); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }
    .claim {
      border-left: 2px solid var(--c-brand);
      padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 1rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
      color: var(--c-text);
    }
    .points { padding-left: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .points li { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; color: var(--c-muted); }
    .points strong { color: var(--c-text); }
    .muted { color: var(--c-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  </style>
</Layout>
